{#- One rule, one sentence, for the model rather than the reviewer.

    Every sentence is the child template's core clause, then the qualifiers,
    then one full stop. The qualifiers come AFTER the core so that a HARD rule
    with no window renders byte for byte what the 2026-09-01 f-string compiler
    did (tests/test_csp.py pins that), and a rule WITH a window reads as the old
    sentence plus its schedule instead of a permanent ban - the defect the
    2026-10-05 audit found (WP2-05: nfz-school is Mon-Fri only). A soft rule
    gains " (soft limit)", a deliberate change from the old text, which gave
    it the same "Never" as a hard rule (no shipped fixture has a soft rule).

    Grant: Prefix Compiler PDF p5, "Always-emitted, templated, never free-form."
-#}
{% block core %}{% endblock %}{% if window %} (in force {{ window }}){% endif %}{% if soft %} (soft limit){% endif %}{% if show_priority %} [{{ priority }}]{% endif %}.
